Z||000007||erikred||12-03-2001||11:14 AM||||I've been tempted by this same swap. My local yard has a few of these, but none of them run. The biggest thing holding me back (other than wanting to build up the Duke)is the fact that the starter is on the wrong side of the block. Since you plan on using the 2.0 tranny, I would think it would be a fairly easy swap.<P>BTW, the 2.0 turbo puts out 165hp and I have heard it can be easily tuned to 200hp. Just turning up the boost should give a good gain.<P>Let me know if you decide to do it how it turns out.<P>Erik-<p>[This message has been edited by erikred (edited 12-03-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000008||RedHaze86SD4||12-03-2001||02:42 PM||||UGH!! I hate it when life start throwin you around.  OK!! I got, errr I think I got the complete setup minus the existing block but they gave me another one to use... total of the afore mentioned parts came out to $300??? instead of the quoted $450. BUT, my down fall is that I can't go get it right now because I'm having to move my trailer house and everything onto a 3-5 acre lot I'm trying to buy. But I'm hoping to be able to do a full swap -=keep your fingers crossed=- within 2 maybe 3 months. I just picked up an 87 auto that needs (temporarily) the block outa my RedHaze project. So lets see how tied up in wires I get  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||Formula 18||12-03-2001||08:58 PM||||Some one used to have a article one these. You could get one from Red Line Racing er something like tat. It was the andretti fiero i think. Impresive. There was another 5 page that compared Millerwoods turbo set up to this and both were quicker than stock. <P>I'd like to see it done but there are a few problems i can think of. I think that the torque sturt is on the wrong side. Also the bellhouse has a diffrent bolt patter so you's have to find a matching tranny to do it. <P><BR>Brian ||||reg||1
